{title: 599 - Rejoice, Rejoice, Believers}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #599 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 599}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]Rejoice, re[A]joice, be[Bm]liev[D]ers,
And [Em7]let your [A7]lights ap[D]pear:
[A]The [D]evening [A]is ad[E7]vancing,
And [F#m]dark[Bm]er [A]night [E7]is [A]near.
[A7]The [D]Bridegroom [A7]is [D]aris[A]ing,
[A7]And [D]soon He [A7]draw[D]eth [A]nigh.
Up, [D]pray, and watch, and [A]wres[G]tle,
[Fdim7]At[D]midnight [A7]comes the [D]cry.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]The watchers [A]on the [Bm]mountain proclaim [D]the Bride-groom near.
[Em7]Go, meet Him [A7]as He cometh, [D]with hallelujahs clear.
[A]The marriage [D]feast is waiting, [A]the gates [E7]wide open stand;
[F#m]Up, up, [Bm]you heirs [A]of glory, [E7]the Bride-groom [A]is at hand.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]You saints [A]who here in [Bm]patience your cross [D]and suff'rings bore,
[Em7]Shall live and [A7]reign forever, when [D]sorrow is no more.
[A]Upon the [D]throne of glory [A]the Lamb [E7]you shall behold,
[F#m]In [Bm]triumph cast [A]before Him [E7]your diadems [A]of gold!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[D]Our hope [A]and expectation, [Bm]O Jesus, [D]now appear;
[Em7]Arise, O sun [A7]so longed for, [D]o'er this benighted sphere!
[A]With hearts [D]and hands uplifted, [A]we plead, O [E7]Lord, to see
[F#m]The day [Bm]of earth's [A]redemption that [E7]brings us [A]unto Thee.
{end_of_verse}
